  "Number": 22,
  "Question": "Successive discounts of \\(10\\%\\) and \\(20\\%\\) are equivalent to a single discount of:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(30\\%\\)",
    "B": "\\(15\\%\\)",
    "C": "\\(72\\%\\)",
    "D": "\\(28\\%\\)",
    "E": "None of these"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each discount applies to the price remaining after the previous discount. Let \\(P>0\\) be the original price. The first discount leaves \\(90\\%\\) of it, or \\(0.90P\\). The second leaves \\(80\\%\\) of that amount:\n\\[\n0.80(0.90P)=0.72P.\n\\]\nThus the total reduction is \\(P-0.72P=0.28P\\), which is \\(28\\%\\) of the original price. The equivalent single discount is \\(\\boxed{28\\%}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
